title: Exact Trig Values
subject: Maths
level: GCSE
emoji: 📈
front-template: What is {}?
description: The exact values of sin, cos and tan you need without a calculator.
---
sin 0° :: 0
sin 30° :: 1/2
sin 45° :: √2/2
sin 60° :: √3/2
sin 90° :: 1
cos 0° :: 1
cos 30° :: √3/2
cos 45° :: √2/2
cos 60° :: 1/2
cos 90° :: 0
tan 0° :: 0
tan 30° :: √3/3 (= 1/√3)
tan 45° :: 1
tan 60° :: √3
tan 90° :: Undefined
sin²θ + cos²θ = ? :: 1
tan θ = ? in terms of sin and cos :: sin θ ÷ cos θ
What is the maximum value of sin x? :: 1
What is the period of y = sin x? :: 360°
At what angle does y = tan x have its first asymptote? :: 90°
